   surrounding text: Good Morning, I have received the following response from contentstack, let me know if we still need a demo from the team. Navigation inside Live Preview returns "Page Not Found" This is expected if the application's routing doesn't map 1:1 with the entry's url field. By default, Live Preview constructs the preview URL using the environment's Base URL and the entry's url field, which works for the root entry but may not work for custom or nested routes. For applications with a custom directory structure, the following are recommended: · Custom Preview URLs – Configure pattern-based preview URLs under Settings → Visual Experience → Preview URL . This supports placeholders such as /blog/{{entry.category}}/{{entry.slug}} , nested paths, taxonomy-driven URLs, and Base URL aliases for multiple hostnames. https://www.contentstack.com/docs/developers/set-up-live-preview/custom-preview-urls · Page Context – Call setPageContext() on each page to provide the current entryUid and contentTypeUid . This is the recommended approach when pages cannot be mapped directly from the entry's url field. This feature requires Live Preview Utils v4.4.4+ . https://www.contentstack.com/docs/developers/set-up-visual-builder/set-up-visual-builder-for-your-website Additionally, please verify that the website allows iframe embedding on all routes , not just the root page. If X-Frame-Options , Content-Security-Policy (frame-ancestors) , or a hard navigation redirects to a different host than the configured Base URL, the iframe will fail to load. https://www.contentstack.com/docs/content-managers/author-content/limitations-of-live-preview Live Preview button not working Please ask the customer to enable Display Setup Status under Settings → Live Preview . This runs the onboarding validation checks and reports the exact configuration issue instead of requiring manual troubleshooting. https://www.contentstack.com/docs/developers/set-up-live-preview/live-preview-onboarding-and-tr